I'd quibble and say yes; I'm the same person I was 5 years ago, even
though all the atoms in my body may have changed since then.[1] It's
the form, not the materials, that determines identity.  But this
example could easily be changed to one that I wouldn't quibble with.
(e.g., gradually change the shape until it becomes a house.)

[1] Not entirely true, but the extent to which it's not true is mainly
determined by my experiences since then, not the change in materials.

